Q1. @dataclass(frozen=True) class Attempt with "attempt_id=str" etc.
    What is the error in Attempt(attempt_id='1', subscription_id='1',
    occurred_at=0, result=AttemptResult.FAILURE)?
================================================================================
A1. TypeError: Attempt.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'attempt_id'

    Cause: the class body uses "=" where @dataclass requires ":".
      - attempt_id = str creates a class attribute holding the str type object.
      - @dataclass builds fields from __annotations__, so
        dataclasses.fields(Attempt) returns ().
      - With zero fields the generated __init__ accepts only self.

    Fix:
        @dataclass(frozen=True)
        class Attempt:
            attempt_id: str
            subscription_id: str
            occurred_at: int
            result: AttemptResult


