Q10. Does Python have a sorted set?
================================================================================
A10. No sorted set in the stdlib. set is a hash set with arbitrary order.

     Sort once at the end        -> sorted(set(xs))
     Dedup keeping insert order  -> list(dict.fromkeys(xs))
     Stay sorted across inserts  -> sortedcontainers.SortedSet (third party)
     Keep a list sorted          -> bisect.insort(xs, item)

     For failure_attempt_ids the order is chronological, not by ID value, so
     sorting the IDs would be wrong. Dedup preserving append order:
        seen = set(); failures = []
        for a in attempts_sorted_by_time:
            if a.attempt_id not in seen:
                seen.add(a.attempt_id); failures.append(a.attempt_id)


