Q11. x = [7, 5, 1, 4, 8, 3] -- sort while I insert
================================================================================
A11. import bisect
     x = []
     for n in [7, 5, 1, 4, 8, 3]:
         bisect.insort(x, n)
     # 7 -> [7] -> [5,7] -> [1,5,7] -> [1,4,5,7] -> [1,4,5,7,8] -> [1,3,4,5,7,8]

     insort_left / insort_right control the side for equal values.
     key= supported since Python 3.10.
     Repeated insort costs O(n^2) in shifting; sorted() once is O(n log n).


