Q12. And if x = [Child(age=7), ...]? Sorted by age.
================================================================================
A12. Sort all at once:
         x.sort(key=lambda c: c.age)
         from operator import attrgetter
         x.sort(key=attrgetter("age"))
         x.sort(key=attrgetter("age", "name"))     # tie-break
         x.sort(key=attrgetter("age"), reverse=True)

     Insert one at a time (Python 3.10+):
         bisect.insort(x, Child(age=6), key=lambda c: c.age)

     Make the class sort itself:
         @dataclass(order=True)
         class Child:
             age: int      # field order defines comparison order
             name: str
     Then sorted(x) and bisect.insort(x, c) need no key.


