Q16. In a list, how do I pop the first element?
================================================================================
A16. first = xs.pop(0)     # removes and returns; IndexError if empty
     first = xs[0]         # read without removing
     head, *rest = xs      # first plus a new list with the remainder

     xs.pop() with no argument takes the LAST element.
     xs.pop(0) is O(n) because everything shifts left.

     Queue-style:
         from collections import deque
         queue = deque(attempts)
         a = queue.popleft()      # O(1)


