Q18. How to push an element to a tuple?
================================================================================
A18. Tuples are immutable; you build a new one:
         t = t + (x,)
         t += (x,)
         t = (*t, x)
         t = (x, *t)

     The trailing comma makes it a tuple: (x) is just x, so t + ('1') raises
     TypeError: can only concatenate tuple.
     Each += copies the whole tuple: O(n^2) in a loop.

     Pattern: accumulate in a list, freeze once with tuple(failures).
     RecoveryEpisode is frozen=True, and a frozen dataclass is only truly
     immutable (and hashable) when its fields are immutable too.


