Q19. Does Python have a ternary ? :
================================================================================
A19. Yes, value first, condition in the middle:
         status = EpisodeStatus.RECOVERED if recovered else EpisodeStatus.EXPIRED

     c ? a : b   ->  a if c else b
     x ?? y      ->  x if x is not None else y
     x || y      ->  x or y

     else is MANDATORY (this was the comprehension error in Q5).
     It is an expression, so it works in arguments, f-strings, comprehensions.
     "or" as a default fires on any falsy value: count or 10 returns 10 when
     count is 0.


