Q21. Can a frozen dataclass field be assigned after instantiation?
================================================================================
A21. No. frozen=True generates a __setattr__ that raises FrozenInstanceError
     for EVERY field; the annotated type makes no difference.

     What frozen covers:
       - Rebinding the attribute is blocked.
       - Mutating the value in place is not. A tuple has no mutating methods,
         so the field is genuinely immutable; a list field would still be
         appendable.

     Escape hatch, legitimate only inside __post_init__:
         object.__setattr__(self, "deadline", self.started_at + WINDOW)
     Outside __post_init__ it defeats the guarantee and breaks hashing if the
     object is already a dict key or in a set.


